  "body": "The P111 decoder's smaller local COPY cost does not by itself pay for delivery\nof its changed query from the existing U8 gather rows. This adds a scoped\nnegative result for a query inserted after U8 section A, with the old rows,\nlater frame contracts, and helper widths fixed, and with no mixing between\nnew carriers before the query hyperplane.\n\nReview files: [Proof and scope](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/ed5424aa3b6ca32fd5bb2c33a8e6afcd87170160/research/shared-carrier-host/PROOF.md) \u00b7 [Evidence](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/ed5424aa3b6ca32fd5bb2c33a8e6afcd87170160/research/shared-carrier-host/RESULT.json) \u00b7 [Source pins and credit](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/ed5424aa3b6ca32fd5bb2c33a8e6afcd87170160/research/shared-carrier-host/SOURCES.json).\n\nFor all 112 punctures, exact rational elimination gives a unique expression\nin the eligible old rows. Their required frames are pairwise incomparable and\ncannot advance inside the query hyperplane while preserving the old tail.\nThe minimum transport profiles are `10 H5 + 6 H6`, `8 H5 + 10 H6`, or `26 H6`.\n\nA favorable complete moment bound gives free entrance frames, no separate\ncentre charge, free compensation and interface work, and pooled fractional\nrank-48 idle space. It credits each puncture's actual source and target paths,\nplus the `H8 -> H7` COPY saving. Every case still exceeds one at historical\n[PR #942](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/942) b; the minimum is enclosed by\n`1.00000864736369386816835926810620863001514` and\n`1.00000864736369386816835926935824150131476`.\nA linear volume argument covers every positive replica count and mixtures of\npunctures. This fixed-U8 class also fails at the larger b selected by\n[PR #1042](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1042) at the recorded refresh. The proof does not apply to [PR #1042](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1042)'s word.\n\nReproduce with the standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/shared-carrier-host/verify.py --out /tmp/shared-carrier-host-result.json\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_SCOPED_FROZEN_U8_GATHER_OBSTRUCTION`. The command reconstructs\nraw U8 from the pinned [PR #799](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/799) archive and U8 recipe. It checks all root/label\npairings, frame paths, unique row expressions, antichains, actual data-path\ncredits, and rational cost intervals. It compares power intervals against the\nretained independent engine. Controls cover wrong query coefficients,\ncoalesced paths, old-row advances, and a mixed label chart. The free-query\ncontrol passes, so the transport charge is decisive.\n\nBase: [abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf). The [PR #1060](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1060) source head is\n[d27499553138bde007f5b1163e65e71da1b18899](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/commit/d27499553138bde007f5b1163e65e71da1b18899). The reconstructed U8 raw hash is\n`090fd574747fbf9628e70cb9beb792732914cfa52e1df147579fe4dbccc68c5a`.\nOnly [research/shared-carrier-host/](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/tree/ed5424aa3b6ca32fd5bb2c33a8e6afcd87170160/research/shared-carrier-host) is added. The selected frontier and\n[upstream/](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/tree/ed5424aa3b6ca32fd5bb2c33a8e6afcd87170160/upstream) stay unchanged. This is a scoped negative result, not a new kappa\nor a complete multiplication theorem. Changed A/B words, early mixing,\nnonmonotone paths, and different owner geometry remain open.\n\nThe package records the initial direct-host failure, the endpoint escape,\nand the reason for the row-reuse pivot. It credits [PR #717](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/717), [PR #968](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/968), [PR #1060](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1060), the\n[PR #799](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/799), [PR #869](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/869), [PR #870](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/870) U8 lineage, [PR #858](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/858), [PR #890](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/890), and [PR #942](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/942). Prepared for Ali Romman (@aliromman) with\nsubstantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0; no independent human review\nis claimed.\n",
